== Trivia ==
*Each Century Cake's name and their respective effect is a reference to something related to Hypixel:
**The {{Item|Crab-Colored Century Cake}} is a reference to the {{Item|Pink Crab Hat of Celebration|text=Crab Hat of Celebration}}, which is also given out by {{NPCSprite|Simon}}. It likely gives a {{Stat|HP}} bonus as most crabs are red, like the stat.
**The {{Item|Pet Rock Century Cake}} is a reference to the {{Item|Rock Pet}}, which has a very high {{Stat|Def}} stat.
**The {{Item|Fruit Century Cake}} (formerly known as aPunch Century Cake) is a reference to {{RN|a|aPunch}}. It gives {{Stat|Str|+2}} due to {{Stat|Str}} making punches stronger.
**The {{Item|Potato-Style Century Cake}} is a reference to [https://www.youtube.com/user/technothepig Technoblade] and [[The Great Potato War]]. Its stat bonus references Technoblade's obsession with {{Stat|Spd}}.
**The {{Item|Barry Century Cake}} is a reference to the now-retired mayoral candidate {{NPCSprite|Candidate Barry}}, who was a wizard specializing in {{Stat|Int}}.
**The {{Item|Sea Emperor Century Cake}} gives {{Stat|SCC}} due to the {{MobSprite|Sea Emperor;Sea Creature}} it is named after.
**The {{Item|Century Cake of the Next Dungeon Floor}} giving {{Stat|MF|+1}} is a reference to many rare drops being found in [[Dungeons]]. It also teased the release of [[The Catacombs - Floor VII]].
**The {{Item|Latest Update Century Cake}} giving {{Stat|ferocity|+2}} is a reference to {{Stat|Ferocity}} being the most recently added stat in the game during the release of the Century Cakes.
**The {{Item|Streamer's Century Cake}} giving {{Stat|PL|+1}} is a reference to streamers feeling luckier than regular players. It could also be a reference to [https://www.youtube.com/user/calofdutyowner {{RN|yt|Refraction|rank=no}}], who has a popular clip of him having horrible luck with maxed {{Stat|PL}}.
**The {{Item|Century Cake of Hype}} grants {{Stat|MnF|+5}}. It possibly refers to the Hype Meter and the Hype Diamonds in the Prototype Lobby, and may be a memorial of that [[SkyBlock|Hypixel SkyBlock]] has received enough Hype Diamonds to be released.
**The {{Item|Undead Century Cake}} giving {{Stat|vitality}} is a reference to [[Zombie Slayer]], where many of the related items give healing.
**The {{Item|ekaC yrutneC tfiR}} is a reference to the {{Zone|Mirrorverse}}, an area in [[The Rift]] which features items with inverted names in one of its puzzles.
**The {{Item|Corpse-Flavored Century Cake}} is a reference to the corpses found within {{Zone|Glacite Mineshafts}}.
**The {{Item|Starborn Century Cake}} may be a reference to the Starborn, who were mentioned by {{MobSprite|Loras}} as connected to the precursors and the {{Skill|Hunting}} skill in [[SkyBlock|SkyBlock's]] lore. It may also be a reference to the {{Item|Starborn Shard}}, one of the most expensive shards at the time of this century cake's release.
**The {{Item|Long-Expired Century Cake}} is a reference to the fact that the Galatea update took an extremely long time to make and release, with the stat it grants being {{Stat|sweep}}, one of the stats introduced in the Galatea update.
**The {{Item|Hephaestus' Century Cake}} references items from the Diana v2 update, namely the {{Item|Hephaestus Anvil}} and the pet items crafted with it. {{Stat|Tracking}} as a stat is often associated with the [[Mythological Ritual]].
**The remaining cakes seem to have no specific references to Hypixel, but are instead a reference to their color or their stat.
*The {{Item|Not-a-lie Century Cake}} is the only Century Cake that references something outside Hypixel, specifically the series [https://theportalwiki.com/wiki/Portal_(game) Portal], where the player character Chell is promised Cake, but as hinted by secrets in the game, the promise, or the cake, is a lie. This is not to be confused with {{Item|The Cake}} obtained from the {{NPCSprite|Royal Resident}}.
*The {{Item|Streamer's Century Cake}} is the only Century Cake that used to be {{Epic}} rather than {{Uncommon}}.
<!--Editor's Note: The trivia below is only and ONLY for the sole purpose of stating a few players. Do NOT add on to the list or remove this message, or else you may be blocked.-->
*Some islands that have every Century Cake include {{RN|mvp+|Minikloon}}, {{RN|a|Jayavarmen}}, {{RN|yt|PortalHub}}, {{RN|mvp+|cake_hub}}, {{RN|yt|Tubbo_}}, and {{RN|a|TimeDeo}}.
*When removing the {{Item|aPunch Century Cake}}, the chat message displays the name as an {{mctxt|e|APunch Century Cake}}, with the {{mctxt|e|A}} capitalized, whereas placing it, and the item name, refers to it as an {{mctxt|e|aPunch Century Cake}}.
*The '''{{Item|Streamer's Century Cake}}''' gives a purple [[Cake Soul]] rather than a magenta one, although it has the same color of {{Item|Magenta Wool}}.
*The '''{{Item|Pet Rock Century Cake}}''' used to give a green [[Cake Soul]] rather than a lime one, but this has been changed so {{Item|Undead Century Cake}} gives it instead.
*The '''{{Item|Century Cake of Hype}}''' and '''{{Item|Barry Century Cake}}''' used to have their colors of [[Cake Souls]] swapped.
*The '''{{Item|Century Cake of Hype}}''' was unobtainable for a day when it was released.
*On the [[Alpha Hypixel Network]], before the Year 300 event, players could obtain cakes on year 299, while on every other occasion they were obtained on a year divisible by 100.

